WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.158 --> 00:00:02.000
(lively music)

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.891
- [Narrator] Drones that
act like a swarm of bees,

00:00:03.891 --> 00:00:06.433
and others that could
hide from enemy radar.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:08.223
These are some

00:00:08.223 --> 00:00:10.580
of the latest remotely
operated military aircraft

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.014
in China's arsenal.

00:00:12.014 --> 00:00:13.260
(plane roaring)

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.490
- We've seen sort of an
explosion of creativity

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.855
from the Chinese defense industry.

00:00:17.855 --> 00:00:21.580
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.420
- [Narrator] And Beijing
has said modernization

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.860
includes building more
sophisticated drones

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.750
at a time of tension
between the US and China.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:29.970
- They want a military

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.730
that can employ artificial intelligence,

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:35.210
autonomous systems and generally,

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:37.610
a lot more unmanned systems.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.000
- [Narrator] China's military spending

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.264
is lower than the US

00:00:40.264 --> 00:00:43.130
but Beijing has been
dedicating a growing portion

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:46.640
of its budget to drones and
other military equipment.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.100
And while Chinese drones don't have

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.330
as much battlefield experiences
as the American-made ones,

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:52.530
we compared different models

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.720
to see how Beijing is pushing new designs

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.140
and capabilities to
better equip its military

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.173
for possible conflicts in the region.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.450
Since the 1930s, the US
military has been one

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.900
of the early pioneers of
unmanned aerial vehicles.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.920
Today, it flies a fleet
of thousands of drones

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.180
that have operated in countries,

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:13.040
including Iraq, Pakistan and Afghanistan.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:16.844
- Drones are gonna become very
important in modern combat.

00:01:16.844 --> 00:01:17.677
- [Narrator] Timothy Heath

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.300
has been studying
China's military strategy

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.830
for more than 20 years.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.530
And is a senior researcher
at Rand Corporation,

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:24.960
a non-profit organization

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.040
that contributes strategic analysis

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.180
to the US Department of Defense.

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:32.180
Drones offer options
unavailable to manned aircraft

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.910
since they can be remotely operated

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:36.450
or autonomously follow
pre-programmed paths.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.050
- [Timothy] There is a lower
risk of human causalities.

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:41.770
You get the ability to
loiter, for example,

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:43.280
and to use advanced sensors,

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.070
so you can have more precise targeting.

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:48.213
In general, drones are lower
cost than manned aircraft.

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:50.387
- [Narrator] It's these capabilities

00:01:50.387 --> 00:01:52.060
that have made China interested

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:54.420
in expanding and
modernizing its own fleet.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.968
- They are building on what
the US military have done.

00:01:57.968 --> 00:02:00.230
The first generation of
Chinese unmanned aircraft

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:03.506
were pretty derivative of the US.

00:02:03.506 --> 00:02:04.930
- [Narrator] One of
China's earliest models

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:07.680
looks almost identical
to the US Predator drone

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.510
and works similarly.

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.570
Both are remotely controlled via satellite

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:12.943
and can carry missiles.

00:02:14.983 --> 00:02:16.780
But China is also tweaking the design

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:18.350
so its drones are better suited

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:21.980
for wherever its military
is likely to deploy them.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:25.670
Like the Global Hawk, the
Chinese military says the WZ-7

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:28.160
is capable of operating at a high altitude

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.180
to conduct surveillance missions.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.710
But the US drone is larger

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:34.100
and can fly for longer periods of time,

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.900
allowing it to operate around the globe

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:38.740
to support air and ground forces.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:41.210
- WZ-7 probably it is gonna be used mainly

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:43.470
in the region or the maritime space

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.890
in the East China Sea and South China Sea.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:49.593
In that area, the Chinese don't
need as long an endurance.

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:52.440
- [Narrator] What it
does need is the ability

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.490
to navigate unstable weather conditions

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:56.560
in the region, like typhoons.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.500
So the WZ-7 is designed with
two sets of overlapping wings

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.410
that the Chinese military says create

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.033
more airborne stability.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:06.590
Beside tweaking designs,

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:09.870
China is also rethinking how
many drones it can deploy

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.350
at the same time.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:14.460
The Golden Eagle 150B
can drop small bombs,

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.720
and China has said it wants

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:18.180
to use several of them simultaneously.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:19.380
- It's kind like a swarm of bees

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:23.030
where each individual
bee knows what it must do

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:24.550
and can make its own decisions.

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:26.200
If one bee next to it gets killed,

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:30.180
the others will continue
swarming to sting.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.250
- [Narrator] China hasn't
demonstrated these drones

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.150
but showed how the
swarming tactic would work

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.620
with another aircraft.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:37.640
The military hasn't
said how it will manage

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:40.040
a large network like this remotely.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.640
Drone experts say the key
would be to program them

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.670
with sophisticated sensors to
communicate with each other.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:47.530
So they approach the target together

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:49.990
while avoid crashing into one another.

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:52.470
If the swarming drones can
work in the real world,

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:54.240
this cheaper unit could help exhaust

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.153
an enemy's missile defense system.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:00.490
Another creative approach
China is taking combines some

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:02.580
of the best features
from multiple aircraft

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:05.570
to build something that's
not in the US arsenal.

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:09.060
China's GJ-11 is a
reconnaissance combat drone

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.110
that has some of the features

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:12.330
of an American B-2 Bomber.

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:14.130
For instance, a flying wing design

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:17.630
that allows the air frame
to deflect radar signals.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:20.150
China hasn't publicly
demonstrated this drone

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:23.053
but he says it would probably
rely more on automation

00:04:23.053 --> 00:04:24.550
unlike the B-2 Bomber,

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:27.060
which needs two pilots onboard.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:30.624
- Because it's flying far
from Chinese command centers,

00:04:30.624 --> 00:04:32.660
it flies at a very high altitude,

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.630
they would have to program
in some mission parameters

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:38.560
and the GJ-11 rely on
navigation capabilities

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.820
and target identification capabilities

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:45.760
to carry out its strikes
behind enemy lines.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:47.370
- There's definitely some distance

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:49.560
between development and deployment.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.620
- [Narrator] Elsa Kania is
an adjunct senior fellow

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:54.149
at the non-profit and
bipartisan think tank Center

00:04:54.149 --> 00:04:56.570
for a New American Security,

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:59.740
which receives some funding
from the US State Department.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:02.070
She's been studying China's
military tech innovation

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.970
for about seven years.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.210
The Chinese military hasn't used its drone

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:08.910
in real warfare but over the past decade,

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:13.170
the country has exported over
200 drones to 16 countries.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:14.003
- They've been crashed,

00:05:14.003 --> 00:05:16.190
there have been complaints
about the reliability

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:19.051
but as Chinese drones are
used by other militaries,

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:21.480
the data or the insights generated

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:24.030
from those use cases
may improve their design

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:25.730
or development going forward.

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:27.150
- [Narrator] The Chinese Defense Ministry

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:29.690
didn't respond to a request for comment.

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:31.320
Last year, the official newspaper

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:32.840
for the Chinese military said

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:34.520
that drones are a new experiment

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.060
and a growing trend for future combat.

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.830
Kania says the newer models point

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:41.210
to how China could eventually integrate AI

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:43.610
and machine learning
to improve performance

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:45.530
and make them highly autonomous.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:48.020
But that also raises
questions about the security

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:49.870
of any AI-driven drone.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.390
- There are ways that drones

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:53.080
can be hacked, jammed, disrupted.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.220
With increased autonomy

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:58.140
does come a greater risk of failures

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:02.590
that are unexpected or of
systems that are immature,

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:04.360
proving to be unreliable.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:05.600
- [Narrator] Despite all these concerns,

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:08.180
China is quickly advancing
not just the development

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:11.198
of drones but other parts of its arsenal.

00:06:11.198 --> 00:06:12.360
(bomb booming)

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:14.250
And that could increase
concerns from the US

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:15.870
and its allies in the region.

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.280
- With these drones, what you'll see

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:18.250
is that China will be able

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:21.170
to respond even faster
and more effectively,

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:23.630
and it's possible that
the long-term effect

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:25.810
of increased Chinese use of UAVs

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:29.520
to dominate its neighbors
is increased tensions

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:32.076
between China and many of its neighbors.

00:06:32.076 --> 00:06:34.826
(dramatic music)

